Actually use:
kubectl patch deploy app -n default --type=strategic -p '{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "readinessProbe": {
              "httpGet": { "path": "/", "port": 8080, "scheme": "HTTP" },
              "failureThreshold": 3,
              "periodSeconds": 3
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}'
+ add command: ["/bin/sh","-c"]
}'

Simpler: merge patch on containers

Actually for add command — use kubectl set using --subresource, or just json patch with merge strategy that treats command as merge? Actually json patch 'add command: [...]' is an array to add; with merge strategy `{"op":"add","path":"/spec/template/spec/containers/0","value":{"command":["/bin/sh","-c"]}}`. That would append? No, for a dict, add/replace work in jsonpatch. Hmm with merge strategy, add path app/containers...? jsonpatch add array at parent returns merged with array. Let's test it.

But actually safer and smaller change — json patch with specific command replacement. Try adding with json patch merge (no failure).

